course: dictionary
lesson: 15417
title: Squishy and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which is its context. «The mud was squishy under my boots.» Here squishy means soft and wet, so it changes shape when you press it.
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «My little brother hugs his squishy frog toy every night.» A squishy toy is soft and squeezy, and it slowly goes back to its shape. Here squishy describes the toy.
explain: Squishy can also describe a person or an answer. «Mum is squishy about bedtime, so we sometimes stay up a little longer.» Here squishy means soft-hearted or not firm. Ask yourself: does the sentence still make sense with your meaning swapped in?
fact: Squishy means soft and easy to squeeze, so it changes shape when pressed.
fact: Squishy is an adjective: squishy, squishier, squishiest.
fact: Informally, a squishy is a soft squeezy toy; the plural is squishies.
fact: Squishy can also mean soft-hearted, or a bit unclear and not firm.
fact: Everyday phrases include «squishy toy», «squishy mud» and «nice and squishy».
exercise: «The mud was squishy under my boots.» What does squishy mean here? | Loud and noisy | *Soft and wet, so it changes shape when pressed | Very tall | Hard and cold like ice
exercise: «He hugged his squishy toy.» Which word describes the toy? | toy | hugged | *squishy | He
exercise: Lily says, «Mum is squishy about bedtime.» What might squishy mean here? | Very wet and muddy | Hard as a rock | *Soft-hearted and not firm about the rule | Ready for bed
test: «Tomatoes go squishy if you leave them too long.» What does squishy mean? | Shiny and bright | *Soft and easy to squeeze | Sharp and pointy
test: What is a squishy, in informal talk? | A long road | *A soft squeezy toy that slowly goes back to its shape | A loud drum | A large wooden box
exam: Ellie says, «His answer was squishy, so we are not sure what he means.» What does squishy suggest? | Loud and cheerful | Very clear and firm | Very fast | *A bit unclear and not firm
